# Captured artefacts. Firmware dumps are large, and on a CTF badge they can
# contain the answer - keeping them out of git means pushing this repo can
# never leak a flag or a credential recovered from someone's hardware.
workspace/*
!workspace/.gitkeep

# Exception: the WWHF 2025 badge is committed as a DEMO workspace (the user's
# own badge, event over, stock firmware). Everything else stays ignored, so the
# policy above still protects future/other dumps.
!workspace/badge-2025/
# ...but not the carved partition bins: they are fully regenerable from the
# dump via [12], and would add ~8 MB of derived data to git history.
workspace/badge-2025/parts/

# Host-side virtual environment (recreated by the control plane on demand).
.venv/

# Control-plane state: selected target, attached bus id, chosen baud.
# Machine-local by definition.
.badge-state.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp

# Wordlists: rockyou + rules are baked into the hashcat image. Big lists
# (SecLists, weakpass, crackstation) are fetched on demand into wordlists/ and
# never committed - same policy as firmware dumps. Keep the fetch script + README.
wordlists/*
!wordlists/fetch-wordlists.sh
!wordlists/README.md

# Terraform state can contain secrets and the rig's IP; never commit it.
linode/.terraform/
linode/*.tfstate
linode/*.tfstate.*
linode/.terraform.lock.hcl
linode/*.tfvars
!linode/*.tfvars.example
linode/id_esp32crack
linode/id_esp32crack.pub

# The host WiFi scan captures nearby networks (neighbours' SSIDs/BSSIDs), not
# badge data - keep it out of the committed demo workspace.
workspace/badge-2025/reports/wifi-scan.*
